  "instructions": "Read the passage and complete the notes. Use no more than three words and/or a number from the passage for each answer.",
  "teacherNote": "The three-word response limit is a prototype design choice, not a verified official exam requirement. Accept answers without regard to capitalisation. Suggested matches never award Actions automatically: the teacher makes the final decision. Review valid unlisted variants rather than automatically rejecting them.",
  "passageParagraphs": [
    "Captain Mira stood on the deck of the Silver Gull and looked towards the sea. Her crew consisted of six sailors, all eager to begin their first treasure hunt together. They had repaired the sails and cleaned the deck the day before. Although everyone was excited, Mira reminded them that staying together was more important than finding gold.",
    "The adventure began with a map from Mira’s grandmother, a retired pirate who had explored many islands. Mira had discovered it inside a wooden box while tidying her cabin. Beside the map was a short message: ‘I have left something useful on this island. Find it, and think carefully about how to use it.’",
    "The ship left the harbour at sunrise, when the sea was calm and the town was still quiet. Before leaving, the crew checked their food, tools and blankets. Mira made sure they carried extra drinking water because the island might not have a safe supply. She also asked Ben, her navigator, to keep the map dry.",
    "After several hours, Ben spotted the island. A red flag flew above an empty hut, just as the map showed. It helped him recognise the correct place among several small islands nearby. They anchored the ship offshore and used a small boat to reach the island. The crew landed on the northern beach, where the waves were gentle. They pulled their boat onto the sand before looking for the path inland.",
    "At first, the path was easy to follow. Then a fallen tree blocked their way. Its thick branches stretched across the narrow track, and moving it would take too long. Ben checked the map and found another route. The crew crossed an old bridge instead, testing each board carefully before taking the next step.",
    "Beyond the bridge, they noticed blue shells placed along the edge of the path. Mira remembered the same marks on the map and followed them. Soon, the sound of rushing water grew louder. The trail ended beside a waterfall. Everyone stopped for a short rest in the cool shade while Ben studied the final part of the map.",
    "The map showed a stone turtle near the water. The sailors searched the ground until one of them noticed the small statue behind some leaves. Mira lifted it gently. Underneath lay a silver key wrapped in cloth. She returned the statue to its place and carried the key towards a narrow opening in the rocks.",
    "Inside the opening was a chest. The key fitted its lock, and Mira raised the lid. The chest held gold coins and another message from her grandmother. It asked Mira to help others with the treasure. Mira decided to give it to the village school, which needed books and a new roof after a recent storm.",
    "The sailors carried the chest back along the same route, helping one another over the bridge. They rowed back to their ship before sunset, tired but pleased that nobody had been hurt. That evening, Mira wrote about the journey in her journal so she would remember every discovery. The crew agreed that their greatest success was completing the adventure together."
  ],
